---
description: All written artifacts targeting collaborators (commits, PR descriptions, code comments, Jira comments) must be in English.
---

Use English for:
- Git commit messages
- Pull request titles and descriptions
- Code comments
- Issue tracker comments

**Why:** Collaborators outside the original team need to be able to read history
without translation. English is the lowest-common-denominator language for the
codebase.

**How to apply:** Before committing or commenting, scan for non-English text and
translate it. Local notes and chat conversations are exempt.
